---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WallpaperCalculator from '../../components/WallpaperCalculator.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Wallpaper Roll Calculator"
  description="Free wallpaper calculator: enter wall size, roll size and pattern repeat to see how many rolls you need and the cost, including pattern waste."
>
  <h1>Wallpaper roll calculator</h1>
  <p>
    Enter the total width of the walls you are covering, the wall height, your roll size and the
    pattern repeat. The calculator shows how many rolls to buy, including the waste a repeat causes, and
    the cost at your price per roll. Nothing you type leaves your browser.
  </p>

  <WallpaperCalculator width={12} height={8} price={30} />

  <h2>Why pattern repeat matters</h2>
  <p>
    Each strip has to start at the right point in the pattern, so a larger repeat wastes more of every
    strip. A plain or random-match pattern wastes the least. When in doubt, add one roll for mistakes
    and future repairs, and buy all rolls from the same batch so the color matches.
  </p>

  <h2>Related guides</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/removable-wallpaper-cost-per-room/">Removable wallpaper cost per room</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/peel-and-stick-wallpaper-vs-paint/">Peel-and-stick wallpaper vs paint</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/removable-wallpaper-vs-wall-decals/">Removable wallpaper vs wall decals</a></li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
